<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">The above financial results were reviewed and recommended by the ACM and were approved by the Board of Directors at its meeting held on� 11.02.2019.Revenue from operations for qtr and nine months ended 31.12.2018 is not comparable with the nine months ended December 31, 2017 and previous year ended March 31, 2018 as the same is net of GST whereas excise duties (for amount Refer PART I (2)(c)) formed part of revenue till 30.06.2017.The Co is pursuing the balance tax reliefs as recommended by the BIFR for consideration by DDIT in the Sanctioned Scheme of Rehabilitation. The Co has provided the preliminary information required by the Hon'ble DDIT. Pending disposal of the application by DDIT, the Co has not provided for any liability of tax in its accounts on the matters under consideration.The Consolidated accounts will be published for the year ended March 31, 2019 in accordance with regulation 33 of the SEBI LODR. For the nine months ended 31.12.2018, the Consolidated losses of Wintech B.V., WOS are Euro 1.55 Millions (Rs. 1237.64 Lacs) as per its unaudited accounts for nine months ended 31.12.2018. The accumulated consolidated losses of Wintech B.V. are being accounted for in the Consolidated Accounts of WML on an annual basis in accordance with Statutory requirement.The Comp. Committee of the BOD of the Co, at its meeting held on Monday 13.08.2018, has approved the Grant of 15 lakh Employee Stock Options under �WML Employees� Stock Options Plan 2016� (ESOPs � 2016). The exercise price for 7.5 lakh Options (out of total grant of 15 lakh ESOPs) is Rs. 62/- per Option and shall Vest at the end of one year from the date of Options granted. The balance 7.5 lakh Options has been granted at the exercise price of Rs. 74.34/- per option and shall Vest at the end of two years from the date of Options granted. The above financial results were reviewed and recommended by the ACM and were appr